IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tga-devices`

-- Cases for tga-devices.l4: Therapeutic Goods Act 1989 (Cth), Chapter 4 (medical devices), from the seat of the patient.
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the deposited text (and, for the periods, the Acts Interpretation
-- Act 1901 s 36), before the encoding was run. Weekdays were worked from 1 January 2025, a Wednesday.
-- The facts are invented: a polypropylene pelvic mesh implanted in a public hospital, its kind on the Register in the
-- importer's name. No real device, company or person is meant. Unless a case says otherwise, a supplier, sponsor or
-- person that is a body corporate is taken to be a corporation (s 3(1)) and not the Crown, and an individual to have
-- acted across a State border (s 6(1)(b)(i)), so the penalties are reached.
-- BASELINE. See NOTES.md. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Dates and periods`

-- 1 March 2025 and 29 March 2025 are Saturdays; 3 March and 31 March 2025 are Mondays.
#ASSERT `falls on a Saturday or Sunday` (`the date` 1 3 2025)
#ASSERT `falls on a Saturday or Sunday` (`the date` 2 3 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`falls on a Saturday or Sunday` (`the date` 3 3 2025))
#ASSERT NOT (`falls on a Saturday or Sunday` (`the date` 1 1 1990))
-- AIA s 36(1) item 6, s 36(2): 28 days after Saturday 1 March 2025 ends Saturday 29 March, moved to Monday 31 March.
#ASSERT `day number of` (`the last day of` 28 `days after` (`the date` 1 3 2025)) EQUALS `day number of` (`the date` 31 3 2025)
-- 28 days after Monday 3 March 2025 is Monday 31 March, not moved.
#ASSERT `day number of` (`the last day of` 28 `days after` (`the date` 3 3 2025)) EQUALS `day number of` (`the date` 31 3 2025)

§ `Is my implant a medical device (s 41BD)`

-- A mesh implanted to support the pelvic floor: an implant for "replacement or modification of the anatomy".
#ASSERT `Is my implant a medical device` TRUE `investigating, replacing or modifying the anatomy or a bodily process` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The same, declared not a medical device under s 41BD(3).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my implant a medical device` TRUE `investigating, replacing or modifying the anatomy or a bodily process` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Works mainly by pharmacological means: not under (a) ...
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my implant a medical device` TRUE `diagnosing, preventing, monitoring, predicting or treating a disease` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- ... but it is under (b), as an accessory to a medical device.
#ASSERT `Is my implant a medical device` TRUE `diagnosing, preventing, monitoring, predicting or treating a disease` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- No listed purpose: not under (a); but specified by the Secretary under (2A): a device.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my implant a medical device` TRUE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Is my implant a medical device` TRUE `none of these` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- A procedure pack (s 41BF).
#ASSERT `Is my implant a medical device` FALSE `none of these` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

§ `Who answers for my device (s 3(1) sponsor, s 41BG manufacturer)`

#ASSERT `Is this company the sponsor of my device` `imported it into Australia, or arranged its import` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this company the sponsor of my device` `imported it into Australia, or arranged its import` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Is this company the sponsor of my device` `manufactured it in Australia for supply, or arranged its manufacture` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this company the sponsor of my device` `none of these (for example, only distributed or implanted it)` FALSE)

#ASSERT `Is this company the manufacturer of my device` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is this company the manufacturer of my device` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- The surgeon who trimmed and fitted the supplied mesh for one patient (s 41BG(3)).
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this company the manufacturer of my device` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this company the manufacturer of my device` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this company the manufacturer of my device` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Was my device covered when it was supplied to me (ss 41FM, 41GI, 41MI(1)(b))`

-- Entry from 1 January 2010 in the supplier's name; supply 15 March 2014; never cancelled or suspended.
#ASSERT `Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` (`the date` 15 3 2014) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2010) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Supplied the day before the entry began.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` (`the date` 31 12 2009) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2010) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Cancellation took effect on the day of supply: not covered; the day after: covered.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` (`the date` 15 3 2014) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2010) TRUE (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` (`the date` 15 3 2014) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2010) TRUE (`the date` 16 3 2014) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- Suspended from 1 March 2014, the suspension stopping on 15 March 2014: supplied 14 March not covered (s 41GI);
-- supplied 15 March covered.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` (`the date` 14 3 2014) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2010) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2014) (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` (`the date` 15 3 2014) TRUE (`the date` 1 1 2010) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`the date` 1 3 2014) (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- The hospital that implanted it is not named on the entry ("in relation to the person"), and nothing else covers it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2010) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- Not named, but supplied under a special access approval.
#ASSERT `Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2010) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Not named, but an exempt device.
#ASSERT `Was my device covered when it was supplied to me` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2010) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`the date` 1 1 2000) (`the date` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE

§ `What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered (ss 41MI, 41MIB)`

`uncovered, sponsor, harm direct, company` MEANS `What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `uncovered, sponsor, harm direct, company`'s `imprisonment in months` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `uncovered, sponsor, harm direct, company`'s `fine in penalty units` EQUALS 4000
#ASSERT `uncovered, sponsor, harm direct, company`'s `strict liability fine in penalty units` EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `uncovered, sponsor, harm direct, company`'s `civil penalty in penalty units` EQUALS 50000

-- s 41MI(7): the harm does not come directly from the device: (1) does not apply; (4) does.
`uncovered, sponsor, harm not direct, individual` MEANS `What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `uncovered, sponsor, harm not direct, individual`'s `imprisonment in months` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `uncovered, sponsor, harm not direct, individual`'s `fine in penalty units` EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `uncovered, sponsor, harm not direct, individual`'s `civil penalty in penalty units` EQUALS 5000

-- No harm at all: (4).
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)'s `fine in penalty units` EQUALS 1000
-- Covered: nothing.
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)'s `civil penalty in penalty units` EQUALS 0
-- The implanting hospital was not the sponsor: s 41MI(6), s 41MIB(2).
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)'s `fine in penalty units` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)'s `civil penalty in penalty units` EQUALS 0
-- Chapter 4 began 4 October 2002: a supply on 3 October 2002 is outside it; on 4 October 2002 inside.
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 3 10 2002) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)'s `fine in penalty units` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 4 10 2002) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)'s `fine in penalty units` EQUALS 4000

-- s 5: a public hospital that is the Crown, even as sponsor, cannot be prosecuted or face civil penalty proceedings.
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)'s `fine in penalty units` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)'s `civil penalty in penalty units` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)'s `provision` EQUALS "none: the Crown is bound by the Act but cannot be prosecuted or face civil penalty proceedings under it (s 5)"
-- s 6(1): an individual (not a corporation) supplying within one State, with no Commonwealth link: not reached.
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)'s `imprisonment in months` EQUALS 0
-- The same individual supplying across a State border: reached (s 6(1)(b)(i)).
#ASSERT (`What does the supplier face for supplying my device uncovered` (`the date` 15 3 2014) FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)'s `imprisonment in months` EQUALS 60

